      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lecture 2a: Creating New Process:\n\n-> OS is always in Main Memory, but it doesn't mean OS is always running\n-> Context of a Process:\n    - Kernel Stack Pointer\n    - Active resource info\n    - Active Files info\n    - Process State\n    - Process Id\n    - Scheduling Info\n    - Memory Details etc.\n-> This is stored in a structure called \"Process Control Block\"\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lecture 2a: Creating New Process:\n\n-> OS is always in Main Memory, but it doesn't mean OS is always running\n-> Context of a Process:\n    - Kernel Stack Pointer\n    - Active resource info\n    - Active Files info\n    - Process State\n    - Process Id\n    - Scheduling Info\n    - Memory Details etc.\n-> This is stored in a structure called \"Process Control Block\"\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Erl7uyyuVBZAaZux9wH7i",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 951.3397620945907,
      "y": -10117.937232949589,
      "width": 1284.87890625,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
