      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1780987010330,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lecture 5: System Call Execution\n\n-> Each syscall has a unique numerical identifier; eg: fork() - 57\n-> OS has a system call table that maps numbers to respective functionalities\n-> fork() -> MOV rax, 57; syscall;\n-> syscall table is implemented like an array of function pointers and indexed with syscall numerical indentifiers\n\n->SYSCALL Instruction does:\n    - save old SP reg\n    - save old PC reg\n    - save old privileged mode\n    - set new privileged mode to 0\n    - Interrupt Service Routine, fetches the address of syscall handler after indexing IVT/Syscall Table with the contents in rax\n    - load new address into PC which corresponds to the kernel code for syscall handler\n    - executes the syscall handler\n    - places the return value in a specific register\n    - RETI restores previous reg contents and mode bit\n\nThreads:\n\n-> An execution unit inside a process.\n-> A process can create multiple threads.\n-> these threads can run either concurrently or in parallel based on the available cpus.\n-> the threads share heap, code, data and files and have individual registers and stack\n-> Threads have a structure called \"Thread Control Block\" like processes.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lecture 5: System Call Execution\n\n-> Each syscall has a unique numerical identifier; eg: fork() - 57\n-> OS has a system call table that maps numbers to respective functionalities\n-> fork() -> MOV rax, 57; syscall;\n-> syscall table is implemented like an array of function pointers and indexed with syscall numerical indentifiers\n\n->SYSCALL Instruction does:\n    - save old SP reg\n    - save old PC reg\n    - save old privileged mode\n    - set new privileged mode to 0\n    - Interrupt Service Routine, fetches the address of syscall handler after indexing IVT/Syscall Table with the contents in rax\n    - load new address into PC which corresponds to the kernel code for syscall handler\n    - executes the syscall handler\n    - places the return value in a specific register\n    - RETI restores previous reg contents and mode bit\n\nThreads:\n\n-> An execution unit inside a process.\n-> A process can create multiple threads.\n-> these threads can run either concurrently or in parallel based on the available cpus.\n-> the threads share heap, code, data and files and have individual registers and stack\n-> Threads have a structure called \"Thread Control Block\" like processes.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "n3_eBq1vrHXLmLqaqsg4M",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 962.7698673942233,
      "y": -7539.926195706162,
