      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781151116286,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lecture 16 : Critical Section Solution Requirements\n\nMutual Exclusion: If process P1 is executing in its critical section, then no other processes can be executing in their critical sections.\n\nProgress: If no process is executing in its critical section and some processes are waiting to enter their critical sections,\nthen only those processes that are not executing in their remainder sections can participate in deciding which will enter its critical section next.\nAnd this selection cannot be postponed indefinitely.\n\nBounded Waiting: There exists a bound or limit on the number of times that other processes are allowed to enter their critical sections,\nafter a process has made a request to enter its critical section and before that request is granted.\n\n-> Any solution implementing \"Mutual Exclusion ^ Progress ^ Bounded Waiting\" is a viable solution.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lecture 16 : Critical Section Solution Requirements\n\nMutual Exclusion: If process P1 is executing in its critical section, then no other processes can be executing in their critical sections.\n\nProgress: If no process is executing in its critical section and some processes are waiting to enter their critical sections,\nthen only those processes that are not executing in their remainder sections can participate in deciding which will enter its critical section next.\nAnd this selection cannot be postponed indefinitely.\n\nBounded Waiting: There exists a bound or limit on the number of times that other processes are allowed to enter their critical sections,\nafter a process has made a request to enter its critical section and before that request is granted.\n\n-> Any solution implementing \"Mutual Exclusion ^ Progress ^ Bounded Waiting\" is a viable solution.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YmR_bqVdG5ovFD6G2PS2O",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 981.4946333744612,
      "y": -1045.4874793612828,
      "width": 1185.5789794921875,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 537473528,
      "version": 873,
      "versionNonce": 597506296,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781155889237,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lecture 17: Questions on Critical Section Solution Requirements\n\n-> How to check Mutual Exclusion:\n    - One process in critical section, another process tries to enter -> \n      Show that second process will block in entry code\n    - Two or more processes are in entry code -> \n      Show that at most one will enter critical section\n\n-> How to check Progress:\n    - No process in critical section, P1 arrives -> P1 enters\n    - Two or more processes are in entry code -> Show that at least one will enter\n\n-> How to check Bounded Waiting:\n    - One process in critical section, another process is waiting to enter -> \n      Show that if first process exits the critical section and attempts to re-enter, show that waiting process will get in\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lecture 17: Questions on Critical Section Solution Requirements\n\n-> How to check Mutual Exclusion:\n    - One process in critical section, another process tries to enter -> \n      Show that second process will block in entry code\n    - Two or more processes are in entry code -> \n      Show that at most one will enter critical section\n\n-> How to check Progress:\n    - No process in critical section, P1 arrives -> P1 enters\n    - Two or more processes are in entry code -> Show that at least one will enter\n\n-> How to check Bounded Waiting:\n    - One process in critical section, another process is waiting to enter -> \n      Show that if first process exits the critical section and attempts to re-enter, show that waiting process will get in\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
