      "updated": 1781525222793,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lecture 33 : TLB and Dynamic Memory Allocation Strategies\n\n-> TLB is nothing but a cache for VPN to PPN mappings\n-> It stores VPN, PPN, and all the necessary bits\n-> They are usually very small in size\n-> Typical Cache replacement algorithms apply",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lecture 33 : TLB and Dynamic Memory Allocation Strategies\n\n-> TLB is nothing but a cache for VPN to PPN mappings\n-> It stores VPN, PPN, and all the necessary bits\n-> They are usually very small in size\n-> Typical Cache replacement algorithms apply",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
