      "updated": 1781527186235,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Lecture : File System Implementation\n\n-> File : Data in a specific format.\n-> A File System specifies how a file is stored, searched, retrieved, modified etc..\n-> A Block/Sector is the atomic storage unit. Typically 4KB in size\n-> To read or write into a byte or few bytes, entire sector containing the bytes is fetched.\n\n-> In Unix Everything is a file. A Directory is a file with a special bit set in metadata to indicate directory.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lecture : File System Implementation\n\n-> File : Data in a specific format.\n-> A File System specifies how a file is stored, searched, retrieved, modified etc..\n-> A Block/Sector is the atomic storage unit. Typically 4KB in size\n-> To read or write into a byte or few bytes, entire sector containing the bytes is fetched.\n\n-> In Unix Everything is a file. A Directory is a file with a special bit set in metadata to indicate directory.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
